IMPORTANT ERROR-HANDLING DESIGN NOTE
================================================================================

In this final API utility:

fetchRandomQuote()

catches API failures and RETURNS a fallback quote.

Therefore App.jsx will normally receive a quote instead of an exception
when the remote API fails.

This means App.jsx's:

catch (err) {
  setError(...)
}

normally will NOT run for API failures already handled by
fetchRandomQuote().

You should choose one clear strategy:

OPTION A - FALLBACK STRATEGY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

API Utility
   ↓
Catch Failure
   ↓
Return Fallback Quote

Result:

App continues normally.


OPTION B - ERROR UI STRATEGY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

API Utility
   ↓
Catch Failure
   ↓
throw error
   ↓
App catch()
   ↓
setError(...)
   ↓
QuoteCard Error Alert


OPTION C - RETURN STATUS + FALLBACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Return:

{
  quote: fallbackQuote,
  usedFallback: true
}

Then App can display both:

• A fallback quote
• An optional warning


This prevents the error-handling responsibilities from contradicting
each other.


